    "releaseDate": null,
    "description": "Forwarder-side collection of the current Windows Defender Firewall posture: profile state, default inbound and outbound actions, logging settings and log file health, plus a daily inventory of the enabled rules with their port, address and application filters and a risk score. Answers 'which hosts are unprotected right now' and 'why is this host missing from my traffic dashboards', which an event stream alone cannot. Collection uses the NetSecurity PowerShell cmdlets, so it is independent of the Windows display language - unlike netsh based collectors, whose text output is localised. Companion add-on to Microsoft Windows Firewall Observability. Read only: it never modifies the firewall configuration, and both inputs ship disabled.",
